{
  "kanda": "ayodhya",
  "sarga": 84,
  "title": "Guha welcomes Bharata with drink of honey and meat",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga84/ayodhyasans84.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga84/ayodhyaitrans84.htm",
  "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy",
  "introduction": [
    "Guha the king of Nishada tribe asks his relative to guard the river bank and get ready for a battle, if necessary, with Bharata. Then, Guha approaches Bharata with a welcome-drink of honey, meat and fish. He asks Bharata with his army to accept his hospitality."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इत्यार्षे श्रीमद्रामायणे आदिकाव्ये अयोध्याकाण्डे चतुरशीतितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus completes 84th Chapter of Ayodhya Kanda of the glorious Ramayana of Valmiki, the work of a sage and the oldest epic."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2.84.1",
      "label": "2.84.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततः निविष्टाम् ध्वजिनीम् गन्गाम् अन्वाश्रिताम् नदीम् |\nनिषाद राजो दृष्ट्वा एव ज्ञातीन् सम्त्वरितः अब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "tataḥ niviṣṭām dhvajinīm gangām anvāśritām nadīm |\nniṣāda rājo dṛṣṭvā eva GYātīn samtvaritaḥ abravīt",
